{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If she is evil in the eyes of her master.</b> That she did not find favor in his eyes to take her as a wife." "<b>Whom he has not designated.</b> That he was obligated to designate her and take her as a wife, and the money of her purchase is the money of her betrothal; and here Scripture has hinted to you that there is a commandment of designation, and has hinted to you that she does not need other betrothal (Kiddushin 18)." "<b>And he shall let her be redeemed.</b> He must give her the means to be redeemed and go free — for he too must assist in her redemption. And what is the means he gives her? That he deducts from her redemption according to the number of years she served with him, as though she were hired by him. How so? Suppose he bought her for a maneh and she served with him two years — they say to him: You knew she was destined to go free at the end of six, so it turns out you purchased each and every year's labor for a sixth of the maneh, and she served with you two years — that is a third of the maneh; take two-thirds of the maneh and she goes out from you." "<b>To a foreign people he shall not have power, to sell her.</b> That he is not permitted to sell her to another — neither the master nor the father (ibid.)." "<b>In his dealing falsely with her.</b> If he comes to deal falsely with her, by not fulfilling in her the commandment of designation, and likewise her father, since he dealt falsely with her and sold her to this one."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:30.806337198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}